ears later investigators announced  last month they believe harmony was  murdered though her body has never been  found her case turned from being a  missing person's case to a homicide  investigation and harmony's father adam  has also been arrested on related  charges but no one has been charged in  direct connection so far to her  disappearance now coming up on law and  crime daily accused murderer charlie  adelson appears in court as he faces  charges in the 2014 death of his former  brother-in-law florida state law  professor dan markell plus the trial of  father and son paul and reuben flores  jurors your key testimony for the  prosecution in the disappearance and  death case of kristin smart  [Music]  welcome back a judge rules charlie  adelson will stay behind bars pending  his trial as he faces charges for  allegedly orchestrating and paying for  the plot to kill his former  brother-in-law florida state law  professor dan markell who was murdered  eight years ago a judge denied adelson  eligibility for bond at a hearing friday  morning in florida markel had an ugly  split from charlie's sister wendy  adelson before his death as the families  fought over custody of the couple's two  sons markel was ambushed in his driveway  as he arrived home on july 18 2014 and  investigators have long suspected the  adelson family was involved it was later  determined adelson's then-lover  catherine mcbanwa allegedly hired two  gunmen to attack markel one of them  previously pleaded guilty in a deal with  prosecutors sigfredo garcia was  convicted in 2019 while magbanwa was  retried and convicted earlier this year  after the first jury was deadlocked  edelson was indicted in april for his  alleged involvement on friday edelson's  attorneys argued he should be granted  bond until his trial prosecutors argued  against it  charlie adelson is a classic flight risk  he faces charges of first-degree murder  conspiracy to commit murder and  solicitation to murder  and the very real prospect of spending  the rest of his life in prison  after  all these factors the serious murder and  other felony offenses with which mr  adelson is charged the overwhelming  weight of the evidence against him the  lengthy prison sentence he faces and the  very real risk that he would flee the  risk that he would corruptly influence  trial testimony and the risk that he  would conspire with or be influenced by  members of his family strongly support  the denial of mr adelson's motion for  pre-trial release throughout this horror  the markels continue to fight for  complete justice for their son and to be  reunited with their grandsons  the interests of the public and of the  markel family as victims of this heinous  crime support the denial of mr adelson's  motion  all right terry they're talking about  something called an arthur hearing what  is that and why is it important in this  case well it's critical in this case in  the state of florida they have arthur  hearings to determine whether or not  someone who's committed a capital  offense like murder whether or not they  are eligible for bond and it requires  the defendant to actually show that they  are eligible for a bond and there is  that procedure that both sides have to  abide by and for the accused to be  granted bond the defense attorney  basically has to prove to the judge that  there's not enough evidence to support  charges and that the defendant does not  pose a danger to society and that he's  not a flight risk so  really the prosecution has to show it  has all the evidence and that the  defendant is the flight risk and the  defendant has to argue just the opposite  many judges generally rule on the side  of caution and they basically say look  this is a capital offense it's violent  stay in jail until your trial and  hopefully your trial will come within a  speedy time right josh and you're a  criminal defense lawyer and you know  that in general in theory bail is not  about punishment it's about ensuring  someone returns to trial now in this  case based on the facts of this of what  we have here and they also consider  future dangerousness etc should charlie  adelson be released on bond  no  uh despite being a defense lawyer i got  to say no  for the reasons that terry laid out  right you're talking about conspiracy to  commit murder you're talking about  murder for hire you're talking about  lying in wait these are all the kind of  horrible things that a judge would be  concerned with and you're absolutely  right judges are risk adverse when they  hear about this type of a murder they  realize that several people were  involved the planning that went into it  the uh the risk of flight the evidence  against him i don't think there's any  way a judge would uh you know leave  their neck out there and take a chance  on this type of a defendant yeah it's  really something where no judge wants to  as you said leave their neck out there  because if something happens well that  could be on the judge and people would  be blaming that judge as well and no one  wants that meanwhile down in florida  also the trial for parkland school  shooter is set to begin next week  following a week-long break to continue  the defense's case now on february 14  2018 a then 19 year old gunman opened  fire at marjory stoneman douglas high  school in parkland florida 17 people  were killed and 17 more were injured in  october of late last year the gunman  pleaded guilty to all charges we still  expect to hear from the shooter's  brother zachary who is one of the nearly  80 witnesses testifying for the defense  a broward county jury will decide now  whether  whether the shooter receives life in  prison or the death penalty now  testimony is set to resume on monday and  when we come back key witness testimony  in the 1996 death case of kristin smart  his father and son paul and ruben flores  face murder and accessory charges now 26  years later  [Music]  welcome back a georgia man who was  previously convicted of concealing the  death of teacher and beauty queen tara  grinstead will not be granted a new  trial beau dukes appealed his march 2019  conviction arguing the court should not  have admitted his confessions and  statements to investigators at his trial  the court responded saying they found no  error in the trial or sentencing and  denied a new trial or a change to his  sentence of 25 years dukes was charged  alongside ryan duke in the 2005 death of  grinstead more than a decade after she  went missing dukes claimed duke  confessed to him that he had killed  grimsed and dumped her body the two  allegedly burned her body together  earlier this year duke was acquitted of  murder and assault charges but found  guilty of concealing and death he was  sentenced to 10 years now both men still  face charges in a neighboring county  related to burning grinstead's body and  in california jurors hear key  prosecution testimony from a forensic  expert in the california case of paul  and ruben flores as they stand trial for  the 1996 disappearance and death of  kristin smart smart disappeared after a  party 26 years ago paul flores was  reportedly the last person seen with her  walking her home that may night smart  was declared legally dead years later  though her body has never been found  paulin's father reuben had long been  suspected of being involved in her  disappearance last year the father and  son were arrested paul was charged with  murder his father with accessory after  the fact accused of covering up smart's  death and burying her body in his  backyard and later moving the remains  all day wednesday consisted of testimony  from a forensic expert testifying about  the property searches done at rubin's  home she said she helped process  evidence collected during those searches  saying there was the possible presence  of blood in a cargo trailer on rubin's  property jurors also heard from an  expert in trace evidence who analyzed  fibers 